  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nx2 + 9y2 = 40 and xy = 4\n\n**Formula used:**\n\n(a3 + b3) = (a + b) (a2 + b2 - ab)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nx2 + 9y2 = 40 .....(1)\n\n⇒ x2 + (3y)2 = 40\n\n⇒ (x + 3y)² - 2 × x × 3y = 40\n\n⇒ (x + 3y)2 - 6xy = 40\n\n⇒ (x + 3y)2 - 6 × 4 = 40\n\n⇒ (x + 3y)2 = 64\n\n⇒ x + 3y = 8 .....(2)\n\nThen, (x3 + 27y3) = (x + 3y) (x2 + 9y2 - 3xy)\n\n= 8 [40 - (3 × 4)]\n\n= 8 × 28 = 224\n\n**∴ The value of (x3 + 27y3) is 224**",
